    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are the `AcceptanceBase` support and helpers). The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field following the existing derived-field pattern (`membershipNumber`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a small `membershipTier(Owner)` default method holding the single rule:\n\n   ```java\n   default String membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n       boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();\n       boolean unique = owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0;\n       return unique && hasEmail ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe derivation lives beside `membershipNumber`/`displayName`/`initials`, keeping the logic in the mapper's single-responsibility spot rather than in any pipeline function or the entity. The `namesakeCount` (nullable `Integer`) comparison is null-safe.\n\n**Tests:** `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (BRONZE) pass, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.",
